    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Bavarian Alps run along Germany's southern border with Austria. The range holds the Zugspitze, the country's highest peak at 2,962 metres, and lakes such as the Eibsee and the Königssee.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Two areas draw most visitors. Garmisch-Partenkirchen sits below the Zugspitze, and Berchtesgaden lies near the Austrian border. King Ludwig II began building Neuschwanstein in 1869 above the valley near Füssen. Villages keep painted farmhouses and onion-domed churches.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "June to early October is the main hiking season, when huts and cable cars are open. Winter brings skiing and quieter trails. Bring layers, since weather on the high ground changes fast.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
